-- title:
--   Patching datum from a strict-ordinary Taylor–Wiles level tower
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field in which the prime $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $r$ be a natural number, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation, i.e. a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ factoring through a finite level. Fix a finite set $S_{\min}$ of naturals containing $p$ all of whose members are prime, and a family $Q \colon \mathbb{N} \to$ finite sets of naturals. Let $D_{\min}$ be a deformation ring datum for $\bar\rho$ and the minimal strict-ordinary condition of type $S_{\min}$ (deformations with cyclotomic determinant, strictly ordinary at $p$, unramified outside $S_{\min}$, and with unipotent inertia — characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on inertia — at every prime $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$), so $D_{\min}$ carries a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $R_{\min} = D_{\min}.R$ with residually surjective structure map, an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$, a deformation of that type, and the universal property. For each $n$ let $D_{Q_n}$ be such a datum for the condition '$\bar\rho$-deformation which is strictly ordinary of type $S_{\min} \cup Q_n$ and unipotent on inertia at all $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$', with ring $R_{Q_n}$. Let $T$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, $M$ a nontrivial $T$-module, $\theta \colon R_{\min} \to T$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, and suppose $M$ carries an $R_{\min}$-module structure with $x \cdot m = \theta(x) \cdot m$. Let $k(n,i) \geq n$ for $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,r$, write $\Delta_n = \prod_{i} (\mathbb{Z}/p^{k(n,i)})$ multiplicatively, and suppose given, for every $n$: a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\gamma_n \colon \mathcal{O}[[x_1,\dots,x_r]] \to R_{Q_n}$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\iota_n \colon \mathcal{O}[\Delta_n] \to R_{Q_n}$, a surjection $\varepsilon_n \colon R_{Q_n} \to R_{\min}$ with $\varepsilon_n(\iota_n(g)) = 1$ for all $g \in \Delta_n$, an $R_{Q_n}$-module $M_n$, a natural number $d(n)$ and elements $b(n,i)$, $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,d(n)$, which span $M_n$ over $\iota_n(\mathcal{O}[\Delta_n])$ and satisfy the freeness relation $\sum_i \iota_n(c_i) \cdot b(n,i) = 0 \iff$ all $c_i = 0$, and an additive surjection $\lambda_n \colon M_n \to M$ which is $\varepsilon_n$-semilinear and whose kernel is exactly the submodule $\mathrm{Ideal.map}\,\iota_n(\ker(\text{augmentation}))\cdot M_n$. Then the type $\mathrm{PatchingDatum}_{\mathcal{O},p,r}(R_{\min}, M)$ is nonempty: for every $n$ there exist a module $N$ over $\mathcal{O}[[x_1,\dots,x_r]]$, endomorphisms $\varphi$ and a surjection $\psi \colon \mathcal{O}[[x_1,\dots,x_r]] \to R_{\min}$ with $\psi(\varphi(x_i)) = 0$, a surjective $\psi$-semilinear $\pi \colon N \to M$ with kernel $(\varphi(x_1),\dots,\varphi(x_r))N$, and a finite family in $N$ which is a basis over the image of $\varphi$ modulo the ideal generated by the $(1+x_j)^{p^n} - 1$.
--
--   This is the Taylor–Wiles patching input in the strict-ordinary (très ramifié) setting: it converts a tower of deformation rings of augmented level $Q_n$, together with modules free over the group algebras $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_n]$ and compatible with the minimal level, into the abstract patching datum from which the patching argument proceeds. It is used by the two Hecke-algebra constructions of patching data for residually modular forms that feed the modularity lifting theorem.
